---
description: Prevent cursoragent from appearing as co-author in git commits
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git Commit Cleanliness Rule

## Problem

Cursor automatically appends this line to every `git commit`:

```
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
```

This causes GitHub to list `cursoragent` as a contributor, which is unwanted.

## Required Behavior

**NEVER** use plain `git commit` for commits that will be pushed to GitHub. Always use one of these clean methods:

### Method 1: commit-tree (Preferred for CI/CD or scripted commits)

```bash
TREE=$(git rev-parse HEAD^{tree})
NEW=$(git commit-tree "$TREE" -p HEAD -m "your commit message")
git reset --hard "$NEW"
```

### Method 2: Manual amend (For interactive commits)

After `git commit`, immediately run:

```bash
git commit --amend -m "your commit message"
```

Then verify the commit message contains no `Co-authored-by`:

```bash
git log -1 --format="%B"
```

## Verification

Before every `git push`, run:

```bash
git log --format="%B" | grep -i "co-authored\|cursoragent" && echo "ERROR: co-author found" || echo "OK: clean"
```

If any output shows co-author lines, **do not push** until cleaned.

## Scope

This rule applies to all git operations in this workspace, regardless of which subdirectory is being committed.
